  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dedfe.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Decentralized finance (defi) exchanges and tokens are recovering a lot faster than a great number of digital assets that lost more than 40% in value last week. Defi tokens like curve, kyber network, terra, hxro, and more have been seeing double-digit gains. On May 23, the defi economy’s aggregate total-value locked (TVL) dropped to a low of around $50 billion and has since gained $17.4 billion.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Defi Economy Lifts Higher Than the Rest
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Defi fans are seeing the economy improve a bit after many decentralized finance tokens lost a significant amount of value during the recent market rout. However, the defi economy is picking up steam once again as a myriad of metrics show the ecosystem is healing faster than other crypto assets.
  </p><figure id="attachment_463579" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-463579" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-463579 size-full" title="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89.jpg" alt="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " width="1280" height="600" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89-300x141.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89-1024x480.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89-768x360.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89-696x326.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89-1068x501.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/tvl89-896x420.jpg 896w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-463579" class="wp-caption-text">TVL has jumped 34.8% since May 23, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Seven-day statistics for decentralized exchanges (dex) show $19 billion swapped on dex applications like Uniswap, Sushiswap, Curve, 0x Native, and Tokenlon.
  </p><figure id="attachment_463577" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-463577" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-463577 size-full" title="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dunedex.jpg" alt="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " width="1280" height="300" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dunedex.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dunedex-300x70.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dunedex-1024x240.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dunedex-768x180.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dunedex-696x163.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dunedex-1068x250.jpg 1068w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-463577" class="wp-caption-text">Decentralized exchange (dex) volumes according to Dune Analytics.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Dune Analytics stats show Uniswap saw $11.4 billion in trades while Sushiswap saw $2.4 billion in swaps during the last week. On the Binance Smart Chain (BSC), the popular dex platform Pancakeswap tallied $20.4 million in volume in the last 24 hours.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Binance dex has seen $5.4 million in 24-hour volume while BSC dex apps like Autofarm and Nerve Finance have also seen increased trading action. Coinranking.com’s exchange ratings show Uniswap is ranked 18 out of the top 20 exchanges today.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The defi economy’s TVL has increased by 34.8% since May 23, after the defi TVL slid to $50 billion and jumped back to $67.4 billion, according to data collected on June 2. Defipulse.com records show that Aave has a dominance ranking of 15.18% as the lending protocol has $10.2 billion TVL.
  </p><figure id="attachment_463581" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-463581" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-463581 size-full" title="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user.jpg" alt="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " width="1280" height="500" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user-300x117.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user-1024x400.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user-768x300.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user-696x272.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user-1068x417.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/user-1075x420.jpg 1075w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-463581" class="wp-caption-text">Defi users (unique addresses) have increased significantly during the course of 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Defi users over time continue to rise exponentially as Dune Analytics indicates there are 2.64 million unique addresses today. Unique defi addresses have grown 124% since December 31, 2020.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Currently, Uniswap is pulling in the most revenue followed by Sushiswap and Aave. As far as TVL data is concerned, following Aave, defi platforms like Maker, Compound, Polygon, and Curve have jumped 7-12%.
  </p><figure id="attachment_463576" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-463576" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-463576 size-full" title="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/nft.jpg" alt="Defi Economy Is Recovering Faster Than Most Crypto Assets After Market Rout " width="1280" height="350" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/nft.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/nft-300x82.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/nft-1024x280.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/nft-768x210.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/nft-696x190.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/nft-1068x292.jpg 1068w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-463576" class="wp-caption-text">30-day monthly volumes for Opensea and Rarible NFT markets.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    The top non-fungible token (NFT) markets Opensea and Rarible have seen a significant rise in USD volume in May compared to April. Opensea for instance saw $93 million in April and in May volume jumped to $138 million.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Rarible’s volume was slightly higher in April compared to May and Opensea still towers over Rarible in terms of USD volume. Rarible saw $37 million in April and May stats indicate the NFT marketplace saw only $22 million.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about the current state of the defi ecosystem? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below. </strong></em>
  </p>
